WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.852
Machine learning algorithms usually expect numerical input.

00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:07.117
One observation can be represented as a vector.

00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:14.887
For example, a customer might be represented as seven visits, sixteen pages viewed, two previous orders,

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:17.942
and fifteen days since the last activity.

00:00:17.942 --> 00:00:21.213
That becomes a numeric vector with four positions.

00:00:21.848 --> 00:00:27.542
When we place many observations together, the vectors form a matrix called X.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:32.517
Rows represent observations. Columns represent features.

00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:37.637
This is one reason NumPy and Pandas were important earlier in the course.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:43.642
A Data frame is convenient for people because it includes column names and labels.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:49.937
Underneath, many machine learning algorithms operate on numerical arrays and matrices.

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:54.860
When you see capital X in machine learning code, think feature matrix.
